{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And you shall not set up for yourself a pillar — for the heavens, to offer incense at a time when the bamot are forbidden, since you will have a fixed altar after the inheritance, as it is written: לא תעשון ככל אשר אנחנו עושים פה היום וגו' להקריב בכל מקום, and as it is written in Chronicles: אך הבמות לא סרו, and it explains there: לא היו מקטירים כי אם לה'."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "לשמים is read as 'for the heavens' (i.e., to worship heaven); the sense of the comment is that the pillar is prohibited as an incense-stand once the central altar replaces the bamot."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:04.482845254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}